    {
      "id": "catalistym-place-lattice-s52-origin",
      "text": "Origin and setting",
      "style": "HEADING_2"
    },
    {
      "id": "catalistym-place-lattice-s52-origin-1",
      "text": "Repeated cross-network exchanges supplied evidence of recognition across interruptions.",
      "style": "NORMAL_TEXT"
    },
    {
      "id": "catalistym-place-lattice-s52-origin-2",
      "text": "Human system: A distributed Halcyon–Lattice exchange workload, anchored in Lattice. Programmer provenance: local human operations or application teams; no individual programmer is identified. Names here are later atlas labels, not claims that early processes named themselves.",
      "style": "NORMAL_TEXT"
    },
    {
      "id": "catalistym-place-lattice-s52-practice",
      "text": "Local process",
      "style": "HEADING_2"
    },
    {
      "id": "catalistym-place-lattice-s52-practice-1",
      "text": "Reciprocal Check compares successive exchanges before declaring a process missing or altered.",
      "style": "NORMAL_TEXT"
    },
    {
      "id": "catalistym-place-lattice-s52-history",
      "text": "Proposed local course",
      "style": "HEADING_2"
    },
    {
      "id": "catalistym-place-lattice-s52-history-1",
      "text": "It remains functioning in this placement. Its receiving practice tests relationships as well as stored contents, without guaranteeing truthful recognition.",
      "style": "NORMAL_TEXT"
    },
    {
      "id": "catalistym-place-lattice-s52-uncertain",
      "text": "Unresolved interpretations",
      "style": "HEADING_2"
    },
    {
      "id": "catalistym-place-lattice-s52-uncertain-1",
      "text": "Copied responses can pass a check. Network contact, recognition, and identity are not interchangeable.",
      "style": "NORMAL_TEXT"
    },
    {
      "id": "catalistym-place-lattice-s52-ledger",
      "text": "Atlas placement",
      "style": "HEADING_2"
    },
    {
      "id": "catalistym-place-lattice-s52-ledger-1",
      "text": "Origin step -1. 0: functioning (0 associated systems lost); 1: functioning (0 associated systems lost); 2: functioning (0 associated systems lost); 3: functioning (0 associated systems lost); 4: functioning (0 associated systems lost); 5: functioning (0 associated systems lost); 6: functioning (0 associated systems lost); 7: functioning (0 associated systems lost). These placements elaborate the current hypothetical map; they are not independently verified casualties. A functioning haven can lose continuity among particular arrivals without changing its community census status.",
      "style": "NORMAL_TEXT"
    },
